    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§109-a, 1321-a, 1321-b, 1321-d, 1321-e & 1321-k, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9673\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in\nrelation to the acceleration of the downstate casino licenses\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo accelerate the downstate casino licensing review and award process.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends paragraph 7 of section 109-a of the\nracing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law.\n\nSection 2 of this bill amends section 1321-a of the racing, pari-mutuel\nwagering and breeding law.\n\nSection 3 of this bill amends section 1321-b of the racing, pari-mutuel\nwagering and breeding law.\n\nSection 4 of this bill amends section 1321-d of the racing, pari-mutuel\nwagering and breeding law.\n\nSection 5 of this bill amends paragraph 2 of section 1321-e of the\nracing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law.\n\nSection 6 of this bill amends section 1321-k of the racing, pari-mutuel\nwagering and breeding law.\n\nSection 7 of this bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe underlying legislation which authorized up to three licenses in the\ndownstate region, was established with the aim of bolstering economic\ngrowth in the gaming sector. This initiative works as part of a broader\neffort to invigorate the local economy through new entertainment and\nemployment opportunities. Recognizing the need to maintain momentum and\nensure that the state sees revenue in a reasonable period, this legis-\nlation would enforce timely actions and decisions. This amendment aims\nto address these delays by setting fixed deadlines for each step of the\nlicensing process.\n\nThe revised legislation is designed to prevent stagnation and ensure\nthat the licensing process moves forward efficiently, supporting the\nstate's goals of economic enhancement through the gaming industry. This\nchange is not only vital for meeting the state's developmental timelines\nbut also crucial for maintaining investor confidence and community\nengagement in the planned gaming projects.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nN/A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nN/A\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of April next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
