    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 72\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 9673-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law,\n      in relation to the acceleration of the downstate casino licenses\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would alter the timeframe for the selection of three remain-\ning casino licenses, to accelerate the selection of applicants.\n \n  As part of the 2022 budget, the Legislature and the  Executive  estab-\nlished  a process to select recipients of the three remaining commercial\ncasino licenses. As part of that process,  applicants  are  required  to\nwork  with  local  governments to ensure that their projects fall within\nthe respective zoning laws of the municipalities.  Potential  applicants\nhave  been  continuously working toward ensuring that their projects are\ncompliant.\n \n  Since this planning process was established in 2022, I  have  consist-\nently  affirmed  the  need  to  operate  a  process  that is fair to all\nparties. The Gaming Facilities Location Board (GFLB) has already  estab-\nlished  timeframes  to  allow potential applicants the time necessary to\nnavigate the process established by the Legislature. The GFLB has  since\nannounced specific deadline dates for application submission and review.\nChanging  the  timeline established by the Legislature would likely have\nthe impact of helping certain bidders and hurting others.\n \n  I cannot support a bill that aims to change the rules in the middle of\nthe process. This is not in the best interests of New Yorkers.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n\n                               __________\n",
